  console.log("Sum of Prime Numbers:", primeSum);
}

sieveOfEratosthenes();
```

This function uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm to find all the prime numbers up to the maximum range (10000 in this case). It initializes an array called `isPrime` with `true` values for all indices initially. Then, it iterates over the numbers from 2 to the square root of the maximum range. If the current number is marked as prime (`isPrime[i]` is true), it marks all its multiples as not prime by setting `isPrime[j]` to false. After that, it iterates over the `isPrime` array to find all the prime numbers and stores them in the `primes` array. Finally, it calculates the sum of all the prime numbers using the `reduce` method and displays the list of prime numbers and their sum using `console.log`.

