// outputHtml now contains the side-by-side diff in HTML format
console.log(outputHtml);
```

This will give you a side-by-side view of the two HTML contents, with deleted text highlighted in red and added text highlighted in green.

This, however, just captures the difference in the raw HTML, and won't handle the actual rendering part (like keeping spaces when elements are missing). That's more of a CSS/layout issue which cannot be simply achieved with a diff algorithm. 

A way to get around this could be to render both HTML contents in iframes or divs side by side, and while creating the diff, for every deleted part, insert an empty element of the same type into the new HTML and vice versa. However, that can get complex and might not work perfectly for all cases."}]

[{"role": "assistant", "content": "In Javascript, it's actually more appropriate to use an array to solve this problem. We can fill our array with numbers from 1 to 100, then shuffle the array. Each call to `getRandomInt` pops a number from the array, ensuring non-repeatability. Here's a solution:

```JavaScript
class UniqueRandomGenerator {
  constructor() {
    this.arr = Array.from({length: 100}, (_, i) => i + 1); // Array filled with numbers 1 to 100
    this.shuffleArray(this.arr);
  }

  shuffleArray(array) {
    for (let i = array.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
      let j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
      [array[i], array[j]] = [array[j], array[i]]; // swap elements
    }
  }

  getRandomInt() {
    if (this.arr.length === 0) {
      console.log('No more unique numbers left');
      return;
    }
    return this.arr.pop();
  }
}

let generator = new UniqueRandomGenerator();
console.log(generator.getRandomInt());
console.log(generator.getRandomInt());
// Repeat until no more unique numbers left
```

This solution shuffles the array first and uses the `pop()` method to retrieve and remove the last element from the array in `getRandomInt()`. This ensures no integer is generated twice until all other integers have been produced. Once all numbers have been given out, it responds with 'No more unique numbers left'."}]

