db.yourCollection.find().forEach(function(doc) {
    var binaryFieldSize = Object.bsonsize(doc.binaryData);
    db.yourCollection.updateOne({_id: doc._id}, {$set: {binaryFieldSize: binaryFieldSize}});
});

// Now you can use this new field for sorting:
db.yourCollection.find().sort({binaryFieldSize: -1}).limit(10)
```

In the script above you need to replace `yourCollection` with your actual collection name, and `binaryData` with actual binary field name. This script adds to each document in the collection a new field `binaryFieldSize`, measuring the size of binary data, and then uses that field to find 10 documents with largest binary field.

