[{"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's a JavaScript function that computes both the median and mode of an array. This function caters for scenarios with multiple modes.

```javascript
function calculateMedianMode(array) {
  // sorting the array
  array.sort((a, b) => a - b);

  // finding the median
  let middleIdx = Math.floor(array.length / 2);
  let median;
  if (array.length % 2 === 0) {
    // average of two middle numbers
    median = (array[middleIdx - 1] + array[middleIdx]) / 2;
  } else {
    // middle number
    median = array[middleIdx];
  }

  let counts = {};
  array.forEach((element) => {
    counts[element] = counts[element] ? counts[element] + 1 : 1;
  });

  // finding the mode
  let maxCount = 0;
  let mode = [];
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(counts)) {
    if (value > maxCount) {
      mode = [Number(key)];
      maxCount = value;
    } else if (value === maxCount) {
      mode.push(Number(key));
    }
  }
  return {
    median,
    mode
  };
}

console.log(calculateMedianMode([1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 5, 6]));
```

The function sorts the array and calculates the median based on whether the length of the array is odd or even.

For the mode, it generates a counts object that keeps track of the counts of all array elements. It then iterates through this counts object to find the elements that are repeated the maximum number of times (mode). If multiple elements are repeated the same maximum times, it considers all these elements as modes, catering for cases of multiple modes."}]

