    }
  });
});

// Configuration of the observer
var config = { childList: true, subtree: true };

// Start observing the document with the configured parameters
observer.observe(document, config);
```

The `MutationObserver` is a built-in JavaScript object that observes a DOM element, fires a callback function if it sees a change, allows us to react to those changes. This way, any new heading added to the document after the script runs will be automatically switched to green.

