[{"role": "assistant", "content": "Here is a JavaScript function implementing binary search algorithm to find the fourth root of a given positive number with error handling:

```javascript
function fourthRoot(inputNum) {
  // Error handling for non-positive numbers and non-numeric input
  if (inputNum <= 0 || typeof inputNum !== 'number') {
    throw new Error('Invalid input. Please enter a positive number.');
  }

  var left = 0;
  var right = inputNum;
  var precision = 0.00001;

  while ((right - left) > precision) {
    var mid = left + (right - left) / 2.0;
    var pow = Math.pow(mid, 4);

    if (pow > inputNum) {
      right = mid;
    } else if (pow < inputNum) {
      left = mid;
    } else {
      return mid;
    }
  }

  return left;
}
```

You can call the function with a positive number like this `fourthRoot(16);` which should return `2` because 2^4 = 16. If you call the function with a non-positive number or non-numeric input e.g. `fourthRoot(-3);` or `fourthRoot('hello');`, it will throw an error 'Invalid input. Please enter a positive number.'"}]

